# KS-1185 F1 — Wednesday's task for Ornith, VITEST, **PRODUCT FIX + NEW TEST FILE** (written 15:53 AEST on 2026-09-17)

Written from origin develop `d7e95cd9f153e9036ed77935a73c93504fa6e3dc`, re-read by `git ls-remote` from a scratch clone. The
product file `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/routes/verification.ts` (1479 lines, blob `28fb58343`) was read at the deps
type (`:114-116`), the default constant (`:127`), the factory's destructure (`:414-432`) and the approve forward (`:1015-1050`).
The held test of the sibling item F4 (`READY_KS-1185-F4`, not at the tip) supplied the harness shape. KS-1185 (0 comments, related
KS-1183) was read. **This task is item F1 only.** F2, F3 and F4 are NOT in it. **PRE-MEASURED** in a scratch clone at the tip; see
`## Premises (measured)`.

## THE MODE — read this twice

Your diff contains EXACTLY TWO files, in this order:
1. `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/routes/verification.ts` — ONE hunk, `--- a/…` / `+++ b/…`, carrying the TWO edits of
   `## The exact change` (one line replaced, two lines added).
2. The NEW test file `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1185-ks-1183-gate-follow-ups-validate.test.ts`
   — `--- /dev/null` then `+++ b/…`, one `@@ -0,0 +1,109 @@` hunk, every line `+`.

Do NOT modify the reference test named in the input (ignore it). Do NOT touch `index.ts`, the deps type at `:114-116`, the
forward code at `:1035-1036`, or any other file. The checker applies the test ALONE at the untouched tip and expects the two red
cells RED by assertion and the control GREEN, then applies your product hunk and expects every cell GREEN, the whole
services/api-gateway suite with no new red, and `tsc --noEmit` rc 0.

## What is wrong (one paragraph)

`createVerificationRoutes(deps)` reads the approve forward bound from `deps.originateForwardTimeoutMs` in its destructure
(`:431`), whose default `= ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS` (15000, `:127`) applies ONLY when the value is absent. Every other value
reaches `proxyReq.setTimeout(originateForwardTimeoutMs, ...)` at `:1035` unchecked: `0` disables the bound (an originate that never
answers holds the approve forever), and `-1`, `NaN`, `null` or a string `'800'` make Node throw inside the forward promise, so the
route never answers. **This task (Wednesday's default ruling):** an override that is not a whole number of milliseconds above 0
FALLS BACK to `ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS`. The destructure renames the raw value to `requestedForwardTimeoutMs`, and a new
`const originateForwardTimeoutMs` directly below the destructure holds the validated bound, so `:1035` and `:1036` keep their
text and read the validated value. Nothing throws at construction; a valid override is kept exactly.

## Where (every bold site MUST change; the (correct) ones stay)

- `:431` — **`    originateForwardTimeoutMs = ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS,` — becomes `    originateForwardTimeoutMs: requestedForwardTimeoutMs = ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS,` (EDIT 1).**
- `:432` — (correct) `  } = deps;` — the end of the destructure. Stays; EDIT 2 adds two lines directly BELOW it.
- `:127` — (correct) `export const ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS = 15_000;` — the default. Stays.
- `:1035` — (correct) the `proxyReq.setTimeout(originateForwardTimeoutMs, () => {` line. Stays byte for byte; after the edit it reads the new const.

## The exact change — TWO edits in `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/routes/verification.ts`, ONE hunk

The fence lists the `-` and `+` lines of the hunk in order, with the one context line between them written with its leading
space. All other context is named here, and every context line is copied byte for byte with its leading space. The `-` line
occurs exactly once in the file. Every line of the hunk is plain ASCII with no backslash.

**HUNK 1 — EDITS 1 and 2, lines 431-432, header `@@ -429,6 +429,8 @@`.** Context above (TWO lines): line 429
(`    createWorkflowInstanceIfRequired,`, indent 4 spaces), line 430 (`    meetsVerificationLevel,`, indent 4 spaces). Then the `-` and
`+` of EDIT 1. Then line 432 as CONTEXT (`  } = deps;`, indent 2 spaces; it is NOT removed). Then the two `+` lines of EDIT 2.
Context below (TWO lines only): line 433 (a blank line) and line 434 (`  // ` followed by 74 `=` characters, indent 2 spaces). **Do
NOT add a third context line below: line 435 carries a non-ASCII character.** Old side 6 lines, new side 8 lines.
**Indents:** the EDIT 1 `+` line is indented exactly 4 spaces; both EDIT 2 `+` lines are indented exactly 2 spaces.

```
-    originateForwardTimeoutMs = ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS,
+    originateForwardTimeoutMs: requestedForwardTimeoutMs = ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS,
   } = deps;
+  // KS-1185 F1: an override that is not a whole number of ms above 0 falls back to the default bound.
+  const originateForwardTimeoutMs = Number.isInteger(requestedForwardTimeoutMs) && requestedForwardTimeoutMs > 0 ? requestedForwardTimeoutMs : ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS;
```

Touch nothing else in the file.

## The test — CREATE THE NEW FILE `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1185-ks-1183-gate-follow-ups-validate.test.ts`

**Harness:** `vitest run` inside `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway`. To run this file alone:
`npx vitest run src/__tests__/ks1185-ks-1183-gate-follow-ups-validate.test.ts`.

The file builds the REAL approve route with `createVerificationRoutes`, mounts it on an express app listening on loopback, and
stands up a loopback originate that accepts the forward and never answers. It replaces `http.ClientRequest.prototype.setTimeout`
with a stub that records the bound and does NOT arm a timer, then calls the recorded callback by hand, so no cell waits for a
real timer and no invalid value ever reaches Node. Each drive returns one row: the bounds armed, the HTTP status, the error log
messages.

**Reproduce the body below EXACTLY as written.** It is 109 lines. Do not shorten it, do not replace any part with a comment, do
not invent a helper, do not rename a variable, do not collapse the cells into a loop or an `it.each`. Every name a cell reads
(`EXPECTED_CELLS`, `CELLS_RUN`, `DEFAULT_ROW`, `drive`, and the imported `verification`) is declared ABOVE the first cell. **The
file contains no backslash, no template literal, no backtick, no dollar sign, no double quote and no non-ASCII character; keep it
that way.** Every string is single-quoted; URLs are built with `+`. The comments contain no quote character of any kind.

**Indentation, stated line by line (2 spaces per level, spaces only, no tabs):** the header comment lines ` * ...` start with ONE
space. Top-level `import`, `const`, `let`, `type`, `afterEach(`, `async function`, `describe(` lines have no indent. Inside
`afterEach` and `listen`, each statement is indented 2 spaces, and the `for` body lines are indented 4 spaces. Inside `drive`,
each statement is indented 2 spaces; the property lines of `const deps = {` are indented 4 spaces; the four `redisService`
methods are indented 6 spaces; the `return this;` inside the setTimeout stub is indented 4 spaces and its closing `});` 2
spaces. Each `it(` line is indented 2 spaces. Inside a cell, every statement is indented 4 spaces; the cell's closing `});` is
indented 2 spaces. The final `});` closing `describe` has no indent.

```ts
/**
 * KS-1185 F1: createVerificationRoutes took originateForwardTimeoutMs unvalidated.
 * A destructure default covers only an absent value, so 0 meant never, and a
 * negative, NaN, null or string override threw inside the forward promise.
 *
 * The fix: an override that is not a whole number of ms above 0 falls back to
 * ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS. These cells build the REAL approve route, stub
 * the request setTimeout to record the bound it is armed with, and fire that
 * bound by hand, so no cell waits for a real timer.
 */
import { describe, it, expect, afterEach, vi } from 'vitest';
import express from 'express';
import http from 'node:http';
import type { AddressInfo } from 'node:net';
import type { RequestHandler } from 'express';
import * as verification from '../routes/verification';

const EXPECTED_CELLS = 3;
let CELLS_RUN = 0;
const DOC_ID = 'doc-ks1185-f1';
const WFI_ID = 'wfi-ks1185-f1';
const DEFAULT_ROW = [[15000], 502, ['originate did not answer within 15000 ms']];

type Log = (level: 'info' | 'warn' | 'error', message: string, meta?: object) => void;

const servers: http.Server[] = [];

afterEach(async () => {
  vi.restoreAllMocks();
  for (const server of servers.splice(0)) {
    server.closeAllConnections();
    await new Promise<void>((r) => server.close(() => r()));
  }
});

async function listen(server: http.Server): Promise<number> {
  servers.push(server);
  server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1');
  await new Promise<void>((r) => server.once('listening', () => r()));
  return (server.address() as AddressInfo).port;
}

const sleep = (ms: number) => new Promise<void>((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));

async function drive(override: unknown): Promise<unknown[]> {
  const pendingDocs = new Map([[DOC_ID, { title: 't', contentHash: 'h', createdBy: 'u' }]]);
  let hits = 0;
  const instance = { status: 'pending_approval', documentId: DOC_ID, steps: [{ name: 'Approve' }], currentStepIndex: 0 };
  const originatePort = await listen(http.createServer((req) => { hits++; req.resume(); }));
  const log = vi.fn<Log>();
  const deps = {
    authenticateToken: (): RequestHandler => (_req, _res, next) => next(),
    mockBodyParser: express.json({ limit: '1mb' }),
    query: vi.fn(async () => ({ rows: [] })) as never,
    isDbAvailable: () => false,
    redisService: {
      getWorkflowInstance: vi.fn(async (id: string) => (id === WFI_ID ? structuredClone(instance) : null)),
      setWorkflowInstance: vi.fn(async () => undefined),
      getPendingDocument: vi.fn(async (id: string) => pendingDocs.get(id) ?? null),
      deletePendingDocument: vi.fn(async (id: string) => { pendingDocs.delete(id); }),
    } as never,
    services: { originate: { url: 'http://127.0.0.1:' + originatePort }, anchoring: { url: '' } } as never,
    log,
    memWorkflowToDocumentMap: new Map(),
    memRejectedDocuments: new Map(),
    dbSaveRejection: vi.fn(async () => undefined),
    ADMIN_ROLES: ['ADMIN'],
    enforceDocumentTypeRules: vi.fn(async () => ({ ok: true, docType: {} })) as never,
    createWorkflowInstanceIfRequired: vi.fn(async () => ({ gated: false })) as never,
    meetsVerificationLevel: () => true,
  };
  const app = express();
  app.use(verification.createVerificationRoutes({ ...deps, originateForwardTimeoutMs: override as never }));
  const gatewayPort = await listen(http.createServer(app));
  const spy = vi.spyOn(http.ClientRequest.prototype, 'setTimeout').mockImplementation(function (this: http.ClientRequest) {
    return this;
  });
  const url = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + gatewayPort + '/api/workflow-instances/' + WFI_ID + '/approve';
  const reply = fetch(url, { method: 'POST', signal: AbortSignal.timeout(3000) }).then((res) => res.status, () => 0);
  for (let waited = 0; (spy.mock.calls.length === 0 || hits === 0) && waited < 2000; waited += 10) await sleep(10);
  const bounds = spy.mock.calls.map((call) => call[0]);
  const onTimeout = spy.mock.calls[0]?.[1];
  if (typeof onTimeout === 'function') onTimeout();
  const status = await reply;
  spy.mockRestore();
  const errors = log.mock.calls.filter(([level]) => level === 'error').map(([, , meta]) => (meta as { error?: unknown } | undefined)?.error);
  return [bounds, status, errors];
}

describe('KS-1185 F1 - an invalid forward timeout override falls back to the default bound', () => {
  it('KS-1185 F1 R1 - an override of 0, -1 or NaN arms the forward with the 15000 ms default', async () => {
    CELLS_RUN += 1;
    const rows = [await drive(0), await drive(-1), await drive(Number.NaN)];
    expect(rows).toEqual([DEFAULT_ROW, DEFAULT_ROW, DEFAULT_ROW]);
  });
  it('KS-1185 F1 R2 - an override of null or the string 800 arms the forward with the 15000 ms default', async () => {
    CELLS_RUN += 1;
    const rows = [await drive(null), await drive('800')];
    expect(rows).toEqual([DEFAULT_ROW, DEFAULT_ROW]);
  });
  it('KS-1185 F1 CONTROL - a valid override of 300 ms is kept, and firing it answers 502', async () => {
    CELLS_RUN += 1;
    expect(await drive(300)).toEqual([[300], 502, ['originate did not answer within 300 ms']]);
    expect(verification.ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS).toBe(15000);
  });
  it('KS-1185 F1 COMPLETENESS - every graded cell above actually ran', () => {
    expect(CELLS_RUN).toBe(EXPECTED_CELLS);
  });
});
```

Why each cell is what it is:
- **R1 (red):** overrides `0`, `-1` and `NaN`. At the untouched tip it FAILS by assertion: the forward is armed with `0` (and
  `-1`, `NaN`) instead of 15000, `expected [ [ [ +0 ], 502, …(1) ], …(2) ] to deeply equal [ [ [ 15000 ], 502, …(1) ], …(2) ]`.
  After the edit it passes.
- **R2 (red):** overrides `null` and the string `'800'`, the shapes an env var wiring produces. At the tip it FAILS by assertion:
  `expected [ [ [ null ], 502, …(1) ], …(1) ] to deeply equal [ [ [ 15000 ], 502, …(1) ], …(1) ]`. A fix that checks only
  `> 0` turns R1 green and leaves R2 red, because the string `'800'` is greater than 0.
- **CONTROL (green before and after):** a valid override of 300 is kept exactly, firing it answers 502 with the bound in the log
  message, and the exported default is 15000. It proves the harness reaches the real forward and that the fix keeps valid values.
- **COMPLETENESS:** asserts `CELLS_RUN === EXPECTED_CELLS` (3), so a file that summarises instead of transcribing cannot pass.

### READ THIS BEFORE YOU WRITE THE FILE

- The file you write is **exactly 109 lines**. If your output has fewer than 106 lines you have dropped something.
- Write every line of the fenced block above, verbatim, from the opening `/**` to the final `});`.
- Do **NOT** write "rest of the file unchanged", "// remaining tests omitted", `...` as a placeholder, or any other placeholder.
  (The `...deps` spread inside `createVerificationRoutes(` is real code and stays.)
- All four `it(` blocks must be present, in order: `R1`, `R2`, `CONTROL`, `COMPLETENESS`. Three of them contain the line
  `CELLS_RUN += 1;`.

## Red cells

- KS-1185 F1 R1 - an override of 0, -1 or NaN arms the forward with the 15000 ms default
- KS-1185 F1 R2 - an override of null or the string 800 arms the forward with the 15000 ms default

## Output

Exactly ONE ```diff block containing, in this order: the `verification.ts` section
(`--- a/Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/routes/verification.ts` / `+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/routes/verification.ts`,
the ONE hunk `@@ -429,6 +429,8 @@`), then the new test file (`--- /dev/null` with NO leading space, then
`+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1185-ks-1183-gate-follow-ups-validate.test.ts`, `@@ -0,0 +1,109 @@`).
Blank context lines keep their leading space; correct hunk counts. No other file. No prose outside the block.

## Premises (measured)

All times AEST 2026-09-17, each read from `date` in the run that produced it. Probe clone = `git clone --shared --no-checkout` of the
Secuura checkout into `/private/tmp/claude-501/night/sdef2/clone2` (script `setup2.sh`, 15:47:55-15:48:02, detached at the tip,
farmed and shared-built by `tasks/code_patch/prepare_clone.sh` rc 0); checker clone `/private/tmp/claude-501/night/sdef2/clone`
(`setup.sh` 15:39:50-15:40:02, `prepare_clone.sh` rc 0 15:42:12-24). Scripts there: `probe2.sh` (one product variant from the
pristine copy in `aside2/`, line-keyed with the `from` text asserted, a test placed, `vitest run --root` on that file, project tsc,
restore with a byte compare, the test moved to `quarantine/`), `variant2.py`, `runck.sh`. **Every vitest, tsc, node and checker run
was under `sandbox-exec` with off-host outbound denied (loopback allowed).** Nothing was deleted.

- **P1 tip.** origin develop = `d7e95cd9f153e9036ed77935a73c93504fa6e3dc` (`git ls-remote` of the source's origin URL from the scratch clone with the source's `core.sshCommand`, 15:40:02; `cat-file -t` = commit). Both clones' `HEAD` = it. `routes/verification.ts` last changed at `fa887f382` (2026-09-17, KS-1176; `git log -2` on the path), so F1's line numbers moved from the ticket's (`:426` at `1125607e9`) to `:431`.
- **P2 the product at the tip.** `routes/verification.ts` blob `28fb58343`, 1479 lines. `originateForwardTimeoutMs` appears on 4 lines: `:115` (the deps type), `:431` (the destructure), `:1035`, `:1036` (python). The `-` line and the context line `  } = deps;` each occur exactly **1** time as a whole line (python). Lines 429-434 are ASCII; **line 435 carries an em dash** (1 of 76 non-ASCII characters in the file), which is why the hunk carries only two context lines below.
- **P3 the defect, driven** (the brief's test at the tip through the REAL approve route, 15:48:50-51): R1 red by assertion `expected [ [ [ +0 ], 502, …(1) ], …(2) ] to deeply equal [ [ [ 15000 ], 502, …(1) ], …(2) ]`; R2 red by assertion `expected [ [ [ null ], 502, …(1) ], …(1) ] to deeply equal [ [ [ 15000 ], 502, …(1) ], …(1) ]`; CONTROL and COMPLETENESS green. With this brief's two edits (15:48:51-53): 4 / 4, project tsc rc 0. With a `> 0`-only check instead (15:48:54): R1 green, **R2 red** by assertion, so the cells tell the two fixes apart. `routes/verification.ts` restored, byte compare equal, each time.
